      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Quantum Computing Fundamentals**\n\n**Module 1: Introduction to Quantum Computing**\n- Definition and historical context of quantum computing\n- Key differences between classical and quantum computing\n- Fundamental principles: superposition, entanglement, and interference\n- Basic terminology: qubit, qubit states, quantum gate, and quantum circuit\n\n**Module 2: Qubits and Superposition**\n- Introduction to qubits and their properties\n- Mathematical representation of qubit states (Dirac notation)\n- Concept of superposition: linear combination of qubit states\n- Measurement and collapse of a qubit state\n- Superposition in multi-qubit systems\n\n**Module 3: Quantum Entanglement**\n- Definition and significance of entanglement in quantum computing\n- Properties of entangled states: independent and dependent variables\n- Bell states and their role in entanglement\n- Quantum teleportation and entanglement swapping\n- In-depth exploration of the EPR paradox and Einstein-Podolsky-Rosen (EPR) experiment\n\n**Module 4: Quantum Gates**\n- Fundamental and universal gates: Hadamard, CNOT, Controlled-Z\n- Constructing quantum circuits with quantum gates\n- The role of gates in manipulating qubit states",
